# Poker rake — an ExactOdds casino rule pack.
#
# "How much rake did you take?" Players ask it every day; the answer comes
# from code they can't see. This program is the rake rule both sides run:
# rake_pct percent of the pot, capped at cap_cents. Same inputs, same rake,
# on the operator's server and the player's verifier.
# The derivation below compiles to provably identical behavior on every
# ExactOdds target seat (exactness PASS), or the compiler refuses it.
# All money in integer cents. No floats anywhere — floats can't be exact.

def rake(pot_cents: int, rake_pct: int, cap_cents: int) -> int do
    mut r = pot_cents * rake_pct / 100
    if r > cap_cents do
        ret cap_cents
    els
        ret r
    end
end

# Audited cases: 5% rake capped at $3.00.
say(rake(10000, 5, 300))
say(rake(2000, 5, 300))
say(rake(100000, 5, 300))
say(rake(0, 5, 300))
